        <h2>The Short Answer: Is It Possible?</h2>
        <p>Bringing family members to Spain on a student visa is more complex than on other visa types like the Non-Lucrative Visa or Digital Nomad Visa. It is possible in some circumstances, but the rules and practical requirements are more restrictive.</p>
      </div>

      <p>The key factors that determine whether your family can join you are:</p>

      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start;">
          <div style="flex-shrink: 0; width: 32px; height: 32px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--red), var(--red-deep)); border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: white; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.8rem;">1</div>
