        <div style="border-left: 3px solid var(--red); padding-left: 1.5rem;">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Registered partner (pareja de hecho)</h3>
          <p>In Spain, unmarried couples can register as <em>parejas de hecho</em> — a legal partnership that grants similar rights to married couples. If you are registered as a pareja de hecho, your partner may qualify as a dependant. However, registration requirements vary by region, and not all consulates may recognize a foreign pareja de hecho registration. Clarify with your consulate whether your specific registration will be accepted.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-left: 3px solid var(--red); padding-left: 1.5rem;">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Dependent children under 18</h3>
          <p>Biological or legally adopted children under 18 years old who are financially dependent on you are typically recognized as dependants. You will need birth certificates and proof of guardianship (where applicable), all apostilled and sworn translated.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="border-left: 3px solid var(--red); padding-left: 1.5rem;">
          <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">In some cases: dependent adult children or parents</h3>
          <p>In limited circumstances, adult children or parents may be recognized as dependants if they can demonstrate genuine financial dependence on you. This is much less common on student visas and requires strong supporting evidence. Always check with your consulate.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--warn">
          <span class="msv__alert-icon">⚠️</span>
          <p><strong>Language matters:</strong> Use careful wording such as "typically", "in most cases", and "may be recognized". Rules can vary significantly by consulate and by region. Do not assume your family member qualifies without first confirming directly with your specific consulate.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Financial requirements ───────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="msv__section">
    <div class="msv__container--narrow">
      <div class="msv__section-hd">
        <h2>Financial Requirements for Dependants</h2>
        <p>One of the biggest challenges with family applications on student visas is demonstrating sufficient financial capacity for everyone.</p>
      </div>

      <p>As a general guide for 2026, the financial threshold works like this:</p>

      <div style="background: #eef4ff; border: 1px solid #a0bfff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;"><strong>Student (main applicant)</strong>: approximately €900/month (current Spanish IPREM: €1,260/month in 2026 — some consulates require 70-80% of IPREM)</p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;"><strong>Each dependant (spouse/partner or child)</strong>: additional €450–600/month (approximately 50% of IPREM) per family member</p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0;">So a student with a spouse needs to demonstrate approximately <strong>€1,350–1,500/month</strong> (student + spouse combined). A student with two children would need approximately <strong>€1,800–2,100/month</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <p><strong>Important:</strong> These figures are updated annually and may differ slightly by consulate. Always verify the exact threshold with your specific consulate — do not rely on these estimates alone. They are provided as a guide only.</p>

      <h3 style="margin-top: 2rem;">How to demonstrate financial means</h3>

      <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
          <span style="color: #16a34a; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 900; flex-shrink:0;">✓</span>
          <div>
            <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">Bank statements covering at least 3 months</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted);">Showing the required monthly balance consistently. The balance must cover all family members for the duration of the visa period you are applying for.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
          <span style="color: #16a34a; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 900; flex-shrink:0;">✓</span>
          <div>
            <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">Sponsor letter from a third party (if applicable)</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted);">If someone else (parent, relative, institution) is sponsoring you, they must provide a formal sponsor letter with evidence of their own financial capacity. This letter typically requires a notary stamp and is often translated into Spanish.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
          <span style="color: #16a34a; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 900; flex-shrink:0;">✓</span>
          <div>
            <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">Proof of income (if you work)</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted);">If you are working alongside your studies, provide pay stubs, employment contract, or letter from your employer confirming your salary.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start;">
          <span style="color: #16a34a; font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 900; flex-shrink:0;">✓</span>
          <div>
            <p style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.2rem;">Documentation for all family members</p>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--muted);">If your spouse or family member has their own income or assets, include those documents too. Every peso counts towards your combined household financial profile.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>For detailed guidance on student visa financial requirements, see our <a href="/student-visa-spain-financial-requirements.html">Student Visa Financial Requirements guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

